  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 108 PM MDT Fri Aug 28 2026\n\nSeveral waves in strong southwest flow will continue to push\nmoisture into southeast Idaho through Saturday. Will have\nwidespread rain showers through tonight. Complete overcast today\nhas kept temperatures from rising and have well below normal\nhigh temperatures for the first time in awhile and this trend\nwill continue through Sunday. Thunderstorms have been slow to\ndevelop today but still expect at least isoalted coverage this\nafternoon. Saturday is more interesting with especially the\neastern zones in extensive shear and instability and much of\nIdaho is in a marginal risk for severe thunderstorms and the \nextreme southeast an even more elevated slight risk. High \ntemperatures Saturday mainly in the mid to upper 70s low \nelevations and 60s to lower 70s mountains. Showers and \nthunderstorms will continue overnight Saturday night into Sunday\nwith most thunderstorms by Sunday afternoon along the Wyoming \nborder as moisture finally moves east. Highs on Sunday again \nmainly 60s mountains and 70s valleys. \n\nNext week expect some warming back closer to normal but still\nbelow with showers and thunderstorms mainly in the south Monday\nand north on Tuesday. Highs in the 60s to 70s mountains and 70s\nto lower 80s valleys. Expect mainly mountain isolated to\nscattered showers and thunderstorms Wednesday through Friday\nwith some cooling expected once again with highs 60s mountains\nand 70s valleys in the middle to latter part of next week. May\nsee some breezy to windy conditions next Tuesday into Thursday\nwith strong pre and post cold frontal passage winds.",
